ew": "Vermont's governor race pits longtime Republican incumbent Phil Scott against Democrat Amanda Janoo in a state that leans Democratic by double digits but has repeatedly elected Scott by wide margins. Eight expert ratings split six Likely R and two Lean R, and prediction markets put Scott's chances near 75 percent. Polling is thin and inconsistent: a September University of New Hampshire survey showed Janoo ahead by six, while other fall polls gave Scott leads of three to ten points, and the most recent survey, in early October, had him up three.\n\nScott's track record of winning big in a heavily Democratic state anchors the fundamentals, and his incumbency advantage remains substantial. Janoo has drawn attention with an economic-focused message and a late Bernie Sanders endorsement, and the race has featured genuine debate coverage on healthcare, schools, and taxes. Still, the combined weight of ratings, markets, and fundamentals points to a Scott win, with some chance the race tightens further.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2101, "margin": -4.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0165, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0219, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -10.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2344, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2363, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2599, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2631, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2569, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1727, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1689, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1678, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1704, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2792, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2255, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1487, "margin": -6.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2939, "margin": -3